# Cline Configuration Rules

## Platforms & shells
- **Primary**: Omarchy (Arch) Linux, bash. **Secondary**: Windows 11, PowerShell or Git Bash.
- Pick the shell that matches the host; do not assume Windows.

## This repository
- One .NET 10 library, `CliUtils.csproj`. There is no solution and no test project.
- Build: `dotnet build CliUtils.csproj`. Pack for NuGet: `dotnet pack -c Release`.
- `local_user_files/` is machine-local scratch (git-ignored).
- Conventions and gotchas for the code: `CLAUDE.md`.

## Conventions
- Never hard-code a machine path; build paths with `Path.Combine`.
- `.editorconfig` is the source of truth for formatting and style.
- LF everywhere - repository and working tree (`.gitattributes`). Never introduce CRLF.
- Commit messages are public text: no user folder, profile path or account name, and never a
  description of content that was removed or anonymised. Conventional Commits, imperative subject.
- Skills live in `.agents/skills/`, tracked and tool-neutral; Claude Code reaches the same files
  through the local `.claude/skills` symlink.
